 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Forms of energy: chemical (stored in food, fuel, batteries), electrical, light, heat (thermal), sound, kinetic (movement), potential (stored by height or stretching), nuclear.\nEnergy is never created or destroyed; it changes from one form to another (conservation of energy). Some energy is always \"wasted\" as heat.\nAn energy chain shows the changes: a torch: chemical → electrical → light + heat. A hydroelectric dam: potential → kinetic → electrical.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "problem": "Write the energy chain for a radio working on batteries.",
  "steps": [
   "The battery stores chemical energy.",
   "It gives electrical energy, which the loudspeaker turns into sound (and a little heat)."
  ],
  "answer": "chemical → electrical → sound (+ heat)",
  "checks": []
 },
